1) Search and delete all the files that does maches the given pattern.

find -type f -not -exec grep -q "your_string" {} \; -exec rm -f {} \; -print

2) Replace all occurance.,
grep -rl 'apple' . | xargs sed -i 's/apple/orange/g'

🔍 Breakdown:

grep -rl 'apple' .:
 
-r: Recursive — search subdirectories.
 
-l: Only output file names that contain the match.
 
'apple': The search term.
 
.: Start searching from the current directory.
 
xargs sed -i 's/apple/orange/g':
 
Feeds the list of file names from grep to sed.
 
-i: Edits files in-place.
 
's/apple/orange/g': Replaces all occurrences of apple with orange
 
